.TH PRNGD-CTL 1 "2026-10-31" "prngd 0.9.29" "Amix add-on commands"
.SH NAME
prngd\-ctl \- query a prngd or EGD entropy socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl
.I socket
.B get
.br
.B /opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl
.I socket
.B read
.I n
.br
.B /opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl
.I socket
.B readb
.I n
.br
.B /opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl
.I socket
.B pid
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prngd\-ctl
connects to the unix socket
.I socket
of a running
.BR prngd (1)
(or any daemon that speaks the EGD protocol), sends one command and
prints the answer.
The socket the shipped start script uses is
.BR /var/run/egd\-pool .
.TP 8
.B get
prints the number of bits of entropy the daemon holds.
.TP
.BI read " n"
reads up to
.I n
random bytes, 0 to 255, without waiting, and writes them to standard
output as they are, not encoded.
A daemon that is still gathering may return fewer, or none.
.TP
.BI readb " n"
reads exactly
.I n
random bytes, 0 to 255, waiting until the daemon has them, and writes them
to standard output as they are.
.TP
.B pid
prints the process id of the daemon.
.PP
The command names may be given in either case.
Writing entropy into the pool is not implemented.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the daemon answered; 1 on a usage error, a number out of range, or
a socket that cannot be reached or does not answer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
/opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl /var/run/egd\-pool get
/opt/amix/bin/prngd\-ctl /var/run/egd\-pool readb 16 | od \-b
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prngd (1)
.SH NOTES
This page is written for the Amix package: upstream's prngd\-ctl is
documented only in the comment at the top of its source.
